	Maxwell's Demon was one of the things to come out of early quantum
physics.  The idea is that since molecules are bouncing around against the
walls of any container, you could have a "doorway" which selectively opened
when a molecule hit it from the proper side, allowing that molecule
through, but being impervious from the "wrong" side.  This could be used to
create a vacuum, manipulate thermal energies, etc.  As I recall, the demon
comes into this to act as a sort of doorman.
	References to it should be fairly easy to find -- I know that it's been
mentioned in at least one of my three college physics textbooks.
